    "message": "Serve saved timeline frames from a cache written by the checkpoint writer\n\nEvery timeline GET decoded, validated and restored the whole checkpoint\nhistory and serialized the world again for state_hash, even for a saved\nboundary the worker had just held in memory. The worker now renders the\nframe when it records a checkpoint, reusing the checkpoint state_hash,\nand stores it by checkpoint hash. A GET for a saved boundary returns the\nverified cached frame with the branch's current computed_until; other\nminutes, older runs and stale or corrupt entries fall back to\nreconstruction. GETs never write the cache, and a failed cache write\nnever fails the durable checkpoint.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
